        "original_id": "fe7519d8-26bb-5673-a9e3-621012c22aae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sila Region, Chad, Libya, Sudan, Central African Republic, Cameroon, Nigeria, Niger, Ouaddaï Region\n- Topics: administrative divisions, national borders\n\nFacts:\n- Sila or Dar Sila is a region of Chad.\n- Sila Region was created in 2008 from the departments of Sila and Djourf Al Ahmar.\n- The departments of Sila and Djourf Al Ahmar were previously part of Ouaddaï Region.\n- Chad is bordered by Libya to the north and Sudan to the east.\n- Chad is bordered by the Central African Republic to the south, Cameroon and Nigeria to the southwest, and Niger to the west.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
